---
source: crates/holst-cli/src/table.rs
expression: "help_of(&format!(\"{line} -h\"))"
---
Save the whole board as a board file, gzip by default; `holst b import` writes it back.
The file goes to ~/Downloads/<name>-<id>.ydoc.gz unless a file is given; it only reads the board.

USAGE
  holst board export <board> [<file>] [flags]

ARGUMENTS
  board   The board to save
  file    A new file, never overwritten and named as given, - for stdout; ~/Downloads/<name>-<id>.ydoc.gz by default

FLAGS
  -w, --workspace ws   Where names are looked up and new things go: a workspace id or part of its name; all of yours by default
      --no-compress    Save without gzip; the default file name then has no .gz
      --object-list    Also save the objects beside the file, one per line: <file>.objects.jsonl

INHERITED FLAGS
  --output, --verbose, --base-url, --home, --no-cache, --help   as in `holst -h`

EXAMPLES
  $ holst b export "Roadmap"
  $ holst b export "Roadmap" roadmap.ydoc --no-compress --object-list

LEARN MORE
  How a board is given: `holst b -h`.
  Exit codes: `holst help exit-codes`.
